// Bounded (back-pressured) channel: channel_bounded(cap) blocks send() once `cap`
// items are queued, until a receiver drains one. A concurrent consumer keeps
// draining, so all items still arrive correctly and in order. Capacity 2 with 6
// items forces the producer to block repeatedly until the consumer catches up.
// (If back-pressure / wakeups were broken this would DEADLOCK — the test harness
// kills on timeout, so a hang surfaces as a failure, not a crash.)

ch = channel_bounded(2)
done = channel()

spawn fn()
    sum = 0
    i = 0
    while i < 6
        sum = sum + receive(ch)
        i = i + 1
    send(done, sum)

k = 1
while k <= 6
    send(ch, k)
    k = k + 1

total = receive(done)
assert_eq(total, 21)        // 1+2+3+4+5+6
print("bounded_chan_test passed")
